{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/261327-wto-ferryman-pasiphae-stats","id":261327,"title":"WtO: Ferryman/Pasiphae stats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-20T10:10:42-07:00","id":261327,"title":"WtO: Ferryman/Pasiphae stats?","content":"Howdy folks, I want to introduce a Pasiphae into my werewolf game as an background antagonist, but I can't find suitable rules for them or Ferrymen. Helldivers just mentions that Pasiphae are very nasty, and the Wraith the Oblivion core book has no stats for Ferrymen. I am not sure where to look next. Any help would be appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T12:13:21-07:00","id":261395,"title":"","content":"Because we didn't get rules for creating Ferrymen until <i>Ends of Empire</i> and they are <i>powerful</i>. Oh and deeply connected to the Pasiphae because the Pasiphae are their Shadows, separated from them to prevent their Shadows from influencing them as carried out their duties. Unfortunately each Ferrymen is still linked to their Pasiphae, not in the same manner as a wraith and their Shadow but they linked. So get that book if you intend to use them.<br /> <br /> Also I don't know what your Werewolf is like but Ferrymen are unable to cross the Shroud, have a +1 difficultly in using Keening, Outrage and Pandemonium and cannot use the Puppetry, Embody and Corruption. I'm not sure about the Pasiphae but its likely the same with them. So if your PCs aren't really interacting with the Underworld it would be difficult for them to actually encounter this Pasiphae.<br /> <br /> Here's the basic rundown on what's needed to create one.<br /> <br /> Attributes:9/7/5<br /> Abilities:20/15/10*<br /> Backgrounds:12**<br /> Arcanoi:25***<br /> Passions:8****<br /> Fetters:5<br /> Freebie:30<br /> No Angst, Shadow, etc.<br /> <br /> The Ferrymen's Pasiphae<br /> Same Attributes, Abilities and Arcanoi as their Ferrymen<br /> Dark Passions:12<br /> Dark Arcanoi:7<br /> No freebie points<br /> <br /> *Ferrymen must have at least 4 in Melee, Awareness and Empathy.<br /> **Ferrymen must have at least 4 in Hierarchy/Guild/Heretic/Renegade Status.<br /> ***Ferrymen must have 5 in Castigate and a total of 5 or more in Fatalism and Lifeweb.<br /> ****They must have at least one Passion at 4<br /> <br /> Honestly Pasiphae and Ferrymen are not really something I'd port over into other games, save for Orpheus perhaps. They aren't really ghosts that deal with the Living World. The Nephwracks, the Spectres beneath the Malfeans (the Onceborn and Neverborn) would be a better enemy as they can and do interact with the Quick and the Skinlands. Similarly Orpheus presents some solid antagonists as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T15:48:55-07:00","id":261565,"title":"","content":"Thanks AkatsukiLeader for taking the time to respond and type all those traits up. I am not totally sold on using a Ferryman/Pasiphae, but my idea was to use one as a really nasty cunning <i>thing</i> that is able to come back only as a result of the Storm Eater obliterating the Shroud/Gauntlet entirely. Wraiths can come through the broken lands easily, and Spectres would be able to tumble out of the Tempest without too much effort. I was interested in having a Pasiphae acting as the being manipulating the hive mind of the spectres to create hell on earth. The Pasiphae is more potent than a Nephrack, but still something the pack could potentially defeat with effort(unlike, say, a Onceborn Malfean).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T20:43:11-07:00","id":262626,"title":"","content":"Again, a higher level Nephrack would be better suited for this. They are much more active in such matters than the Pasiphae who seem more to operate as a foil to the Ferrymen than anything else. If you want a great example of a powerful Nephrack look at Coldheart in <i>Ends of Empire</i>. He's a serious monster and fine example of what high level spectres can do. Of course he's a truly ancient one, having been in life one of Alexander the Great's generals. But you can create one that is somehow tied to the Garou. Maybe in life it was an ancient enemy, slain centuries ago by another pack. Or maybe he was an abused and betrayed kinfolk who's hatred for those Garou that cost him his life has driven him to seek vengeance against all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}